				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5890</guid>
				<title>SCP-5890</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5890</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;scp-image-block block-right&quot; style=&quot;width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5890/URL-GOES-HERE&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--resized-images/scp-5890/URL-GOES-HERE/medium.jpg&quot; style=&quot;width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;&quot; alt=&quot;URL-GOES-HERE&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;scp-image-caption&quot; style=&quot;width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CAPTION-GOES-HERE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5890&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5890 is to be kept in a standard humanoid containment cell. The floor of SCP-5890&#039;s cell is to be covered in a layer of sand at least 10 centimetres thick. Every 3 days SCP-5890&#039;s cell is to be cleared of any SCP-5890-A instances found growing. If SCP-5890 attempts to make physical contact with any member of the clearing team a piece of paper or other object created using wood is to be made visible to SCP-5890.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5890 is similar in appearance to a human female though it&#039;s skin resembles smooth tree bark, most closely resembling that of Quercus Alba(white oak). It is approximately 1.65 meters tall and appears to be pregnant.&lt;br /&gt;
While it is capable of advanced reasoning and speech it does will spend most of it&#039;s time sitting in the middle of its containment cell.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Any contact made between bare skin and any part of SCP-5890 will result in the skin rapidly transforming into bark similar to SCP-5890&#039;s skin. If contact is broken in under 2 seconds only the top layer of the subjects epidermis will need to be removed to completely remove the bark like skin. If contact is held for more than 2 seconds up to flesh up to 1.5 centimetres from the surface will need to be removed. If the converted flesh is not removed within 4 hours rapid necrosis will set in, potentially spreading to the rest of the subject&#039;s body.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every 2-3 days SCP-5890 will produce a single acorn[SCP-5890-A] of species Quercus Alba, approximately 3 times the average size of an acorn from that species, from its navel. SCP-5890 will then proceed to push the SCP-5890-A instance into the ground. SCP-5890 is able to push the SCP-5890-A instance in to the ground no matter what the ground is made of. SCP-5890-A instances will grow far faster than would be expected. The roots of SCP-5890-A instances are capable of growing through any material and do not appear to require water, nutrients or sunlight. If SCP-5890-A instances are allowed to grow in or near man made structures they will prefer to grow into the structures.&lt;br /&gt;
when questioned SCP-5890 seems to be unwilling or unable to answer any questions directly regarding itself.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interview Log 5890-1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewed:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5890&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr Green&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Hello.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; Hello.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; May I ask, what are you?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5890 does not reply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Okay, another question. Why do you plant acorns in the floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5890 does not reply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; After 5 minutes of waiting DR Green left SCP-5890&#039;s cell. SCP-5890 appears unwilling to cooperate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Log 5890-2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewed:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5890&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr Green&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr Green walks in carrying several sheets of paper&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; (retreats into a corner) you would hold part of a butchered corpse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; What?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; You murdered a tree.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Do you mean this paper?(he holds up the papers)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DR Green leaves the containment cell and returns without the paper.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Now can we talk?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; (Moves closer to Dr Green) Yes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; What was so terrifying about the paper?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; You would be displeased by a human head.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; That sapling (points to a SCP-5890-A instance) why does it grow faster than normal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; It does not.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Can you tell me anything about yourself?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5890 does not reply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; Is this conversation going to accomplish anything?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; (Quickly touches Dr Green&#039;s arm) Yes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dr Green:&lt;/strong&gt; (Looks at his arm which now resembles bark) What did you, what is this?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCP-5890:&lt;/strong&gt; Your truth form.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr Green quickly left the room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#171; &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxw&quot;&gt;SCP-XXXW&lt;/a&gt; | SCP-XXXX | &lt;a class=&quot;newpage&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxy&quot;&gt;SCP-XXXY&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#187;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eternalshadow&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6881518&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608692359&quot; alt=&quot;EternalShadow&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6881518)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eternalshadow&quot;  &gt;EternalShadow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 22 Dec 2020 21:06:01 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><a href="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5890/URL-GOES-HERE"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--resized-images/scp-5890/URL-GOES-HERE/medium.jpg" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="URL-GOES-HERE" class="image" /></a> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>CAPTION-GOES-HERE</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5890</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong><br /> SCP-5890 is to be kept in a standard humanoid containment cell. The floor of SCP-5890's cell is to be covered in a layer of sand at least 10 centimetres thick. Every 3 days SCP-5890's cell is to be cleared of any SCP-5890-A instances found growing. If SCP-5890 attempts to make physical contact with any member of the clearing team a piece of paper or other object created using wood is to be made visible to SCP-5890.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong><br /> SCP-5890 is similar in appearance to a human female though it's skin resembles smooth tree bark, most closely resembling that of Quercus Alba(white oak). It is approximately 1.65 meters tall and appears to be pregnant.<br /> While it is capable of advanced reasoning and speech it does will spend most of it's time sitting in the middle of its containment cell.</p> <p>Any contact made between bare skin and any part of SCP-5890 will result in the skin rapidly transforming into bark similar to SCP-5890's skin. If contact is broken in under 2 seconds only the top layer of the subjects epidermis will need to be removed to completely remove the bark like skin. If contact is held for more than 2 seconds up to flesh up to 1.5 centimetres from the surface will need to be removed. If the converted flesh is not removed within 4 hours rapid necrosis will set in, potentially spreading to the rest of the subject's body.</p> <p>Every 2-3 days SCP-5890 will produce a single acorn[SCP-5890-A] of species Quercus Alba, approximately 3 times the average size of an acorn from that species, from its navel. SCP-5890 will then proceed to push the SCP-5890-A instance into the ground. SCP-5890 is able to push the SCP-5890-A instance in to the ground no matter what the ground is made of. SCP-5890-A instances will grow far faster than would be expected. The roots of SCP-5890-A instances are capable of growing through any material and do not appear to require water, nutrients or sunlight. If SCP-5890-A instances are allowed to grow in or near man made structures they will prefer to grow into the structures.<br /> when questioned SCP-5890 seems to be unwilling or unable to answer any questions directly regarding itself.<br /> <strong>Interview Log 5890-1</strong></p> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5890</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr Green</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Hello.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> Hello.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> May I ask, what are you?</p> <p>SCP-5890 does not reply.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Okay, another question. Why do you plant acorns in the floor.</p> <p>SCP-5890 does not reply.</p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> After 5 minutes of waiting DR Green left SCP-5890's cell. SCP-5890 appears unwilling to cooperate.</p> </div> <p><strong>Interview Log 5890-2</strong></p> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5890</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr Green</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> Dr Green walks in carrying several sheets of paper</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> (retreats into a corner) you would hold part of a butchered corpse.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> What?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> You murdered a tree.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Do you mean this paper?(he holds up the papers)</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> Yes.</p> <p>DR Green leaves the containment cell and returns without the paper.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Now can we talk?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> (Moves closer to Dr Green) Yes.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> What was so terrifying about the paper?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> You would be displeased by a human head.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> That sapling (points to a SCP-5890-A instance) why does it grow faster than normal.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> It does not.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Can you tell me anything about yourself?</p> <p>SCP-5890 does not reply.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> Is this conversation going to accomplish anything?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> (Quickly touches Dr Green's arm) Yes.</p> <p><strong>Dr Green:</strong> (Looks at his arm which now resembles bark) What did you, what is this?</p> <p><strong>SCP-5890:</strong> Your truth form.</p> <p>Dr Green quickly left the room.</p> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxw">SCP-XXXW</a> | SCP-XXXX | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-xxxy">SCP-XXXY</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eternalshadow" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6881518&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608692359" alt="EternalShadow" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6881518)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eternalshadow" >EternalShadow</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
