&lt;p&gt;If you&#039;ve created &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;at least three&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; successful&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-989696-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; pages (including SCP articles, tales, GoI-format documents, site dossiers, and artwork pages), please take the time to create an author page and take credit for your work. Create and tweak as you desire, and add yourself to the list above alphabetically by your &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;wikidot username&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The format for your slot is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:75%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;||[[*user&amp;#32;YOURUSERNAME]]||[[[AUTHOR-PAGE-LINK&amp;#32;|NAME-OF-LINK]]]||Personnel||&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See additional entries for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You might also consider adding a chevron from a &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/list-of-foundation-s-internal-departments&quot;&gt;Foundation Department&lt;/a&gt; you are interested in, if applicable. If you have any questions or concerns regarding this database, or need assistance adding your information to it, please contact staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Troy&#039;s&amp;nbsp;Tips&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;Low&amp;nbsp;Maintenace&amp;nbsp;Author&amp;nbsp;Pages&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Title&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;hiding&amp;nbsp;text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How to Use This Document:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hey there! This is TroyL, your friendly neighborhood guy. I’ve had a lot of people asking questions about author pages and ways to make them as low maintenance as possible, so I created this template. The coolest thing about this template? It will AUTOMATICALLY display everything you write on the site, so you’ll not have to worry about updating your lists ever again!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take a look down there. See where it says “YOUR NAME HERE”? Just type your Wikidot User Name, exactly as it’s spelling, between those quotation marks, leaving no spaces. Bam. You’re done! Feel free to fill out the rest of the document however you want, screwing around with it however you please, but leave the modules as they are! There’s a chance, after the tag update, that this template will be further updated to include more stuff, so keep your eyes open.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a note, if you don’t have a Joke SCP or a Foundation Tales up yet, just delete that portion of the document. If you write one later, just copy/paste that part back in!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Final Note: Make sure you Tag your profile with the “author” tag when you’re finished! That way, it won’t show up on its own lists. Thanks, and I hope you like the template!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Template:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
&lt;code&gt;__SCPs__:
 [[module ListPages created_by=&amp;quot;YOUR NAME HERE&amp;quot; separate=&amp;quot;no&amp;quot; limit=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; perPage=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; tags=&amp;quot;scp, -joke&amp;quot; order=&amp;quot;title&amp;quot;]]
 * %%title_linked%%
 [[/module]]

__SCP-J__:
 [[module ListPages created_by=&amp;quot;YOUR NAME HERE&amp;quot; separate=&amp;quot;no&amp;quot; limit=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; perPage=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; tags=&amp;quot;joke, -tale&amp;quot; order=&amp;quot;title&amp;quot;]]
 * %%title_linked%%
 [[/module]]

__Adopted Pages/Collaborations__:
Unfortunately, there’s no way to make this pick up a collaboration or an article that you’ve adopted, so you’ll have to enter them manually.  Put an asterisk (*) at the beginning of each one to keep the default, bulleted format that the modules possess.

__Foundation Tales__:
 [[module ListPages created_by=&amp;quot;YOUR NAME HERE&amp;quot; separate=&amp;quot;no&amp;quot; limit=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; perPage=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; tags=&amp;quot;tale&amp;quot; order=&amp;quot;title&amp;quot;]]
 * %%title_linked%%
 [[/module]]

__ Other Creations__:
 [[module ListPages created_by=&amp;quot;YOUR NAME HERE&amp;quot; separate=&amp;quot;no&amp;quot; limit=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; perPage=&amp;quot;250&amp;quot; tags=&amp;quot;-scp, -author, -tale&amp;quot; order=&amp;quot;title&amp;quot;]]
 * %%title_linked%%
 [[/module]]&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a note, these are all designed to search by tags. Therefore, if you’re a member who has written several guides or been involved in a few of our projects, you might try to “guide” or “project” tag.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-administrator&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=169306&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608692363&quot; alt=&quot;The Administrator&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=169306)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-administrator&quot;  &gt;The Administrator&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-989696-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Meaning a page that remains above -10 for 24 hours after having been posted.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</description>
